findings.description:
`TestIntegrationBeyondDeviceLimit` only checks that a new device is rejected at the limit. Missing coverage:
- an existing device inside the window still gets through when the limit is reached (the `updateDevice` success path, which is the purpose of that branch);
- a retry after rejection, which would have caught the bypass above;
- `Authenticate` returning `ErrDeviceLimitReached` (`client_test.go` only covers org lookup);
- `TagDevice` returning non-limit errors, which it now propagates (`impl_test.go` has no error case).
